# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF. cmd.exe's `goto` label matching is
# unreliable with LF-only files: the `:label` at the end of a line may
# include a trailing \n byte as part of the label name, which fails to
# match `goto :label`. This surfaced in Phase 5c task 0 audit where
# `scripts/brehon/cargo-test.bat --test e2e --no-run -p lemmy_server`
# exited with "The system cannot find the batch label specified - run_plain"
# because the `:run_plain` label line (line 97) was LF-terminated.
#
# Force CRLF on every .bat checkout, regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# bm-runlog.md is an APPEND-ONLY ledger — BM/advisor entries are only
# ever added, never edited in place. Use the union merge driver so a
# cross-branch divergence keeps BOTH sides' added entries instead of
# producing a conflict. This makes the entire runlog-conflict class
# structurally impossible.
#
# Incident that motivated this (v1-ship-1-r2, 2026-05-18): the bm-pr
# step appended a "PR opened" entry on the phase branch; the (old,
# pre-merge) L14 step appended a "bm: merge" entry on governance-v0.
# Both diverged from the common ancestor on this file -> the PR went
# DIRTY/CONFLICTING and `gh pr merge` could not complete (Junior #322
# BLOCKED; DQ #265; feedback_l14_runlog_on_trunk_self_conflicts_with_
# bm_pr.md). The L14 rule was revised to write the runlog COMPLETE
# entry POST-merge (commit bade657f4), which prevents THAT recurrence;
# this union driver prevents the whole class (any two appenders, any
# branches) and would have prevented the incident even under the old
# ordering.
#
# Safe here because the file is free-form append-only markdown: union
# merge concatenates both sides with no ordering/dedup guarantee, which
# for an independently-meaningful timestamped ledger is cosmetic at
# worst and far preferable to a blocked merge. Do NOT generalise this
# driver to structured files (JSON/YAML) — there a naive line union
# corrupts the document. Scope is deliberately this one file only.
.claude/runlog/bm-runlog.md merge=union
